# Reflection (300–500 words) — write this yourself

Worth 5 marks and must be specific and honest. Answer these four prompts in your own words:
1. Which AI tools did you use, and at which stages? (Be exact: e.g. "Claude generated the first version of agent_@@L3@@.c; I then ...")
2. What did the AI do well? Where was it wrong or misleading? (Name real examples from your own testing.)
3. What did you change, add or reject, and why?
4. What did you learn about your own understanding of network programming?

Tip: before writing, read agent_@@L3@@.c top to bottom and make sure you can explain framing (`read_line`, `read_chunk`),
the PUT byte count, the thread model and `stop_monitor`. The lab test and viva depend on this.
